    <description>WHAT IT DOES: Turns a form&apos;s Contact 2 answers (the second person on the form, such as a spouse or partner) into a Contact and hands it to the NPSP Contact engine. This is the mapping step: it decides which form fields land in which Contact fields, and nothing else.

HOW IT WORKS, STEP BY STEP:
1. The Conversion Setup action loads the submission, its template, the parent submission and section for a repeater or table row, and the Contact matching rules, in one read. The Related Records step also dispatches repeater and table rows captured for this contact to this flow, one event per row.
2. The Contact (Field Map) transform is the heart of the flow and the reason to clone it: every line maps one form answer onto one Contact field. NPSP&apos;s contact preferences are filled the NPSP way: the email lands in Personal, Work or Alternate Email by the form&apos;s Email Type (Other becomes Alternate) and Preferred Email follows it, and the phone lands in Home, Mobile or Work Phone by Phone Type with Preferred Phone following. Do Not Contact is set, never cleared, when the Do Not Call box is checked. The address blocks map only when the template&apos;s address sub-rules are on, so curated addresses are not overwritten by blank form answers.
3. The map never sets the Contact&apos;s Account. In NPSP that link is the Household, and the engine owns it: a new Contact 1 gets its Household from NPSP, and in Household mode every other person joins the Household already on the submission.
4. The record goes to the NPSP Contact engine together with the template&apos;s Contact matching rules, and the engine does the rest: strip, match, save, Household, log, follow-ups.

WHERE IT FITS: Installed by the Alternate Contact record of Form Template Conversion Mapping Default. To change WHICH FIELDS a person gets from a form, clone this flow, adjust the transform, and point the template&apos;s override hook (FlowApiName_Contact2__c) or the custom metadata at your clone; matching, saving and Household behaviour live in the engine, not here.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>True when the Contact 2 Set Mailing Address rule is enabled; address mapping stays opt-in so matches never silently overwrite curated addresses.</description>
        <name>AssignMailingAddress</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!Setup.platformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact1_FieldApiName},
IF({!Setup.formSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!Setup.pageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!Setup.formTemplate.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;)
),
IF({!Setup.platformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact2_FieldApiName},
if({!Setup.formSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!Setup.pageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!Setup.formTemplate.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Mailing Address&apos;)
),
false))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>True when the Contact 2 Set Other Address rule is enabled.</description>
        <name>AssignOtherAddress</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!Setup.platformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact1_FieldApiName},
IF({!Setup.formSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!Setup.pageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Other Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!Setup.formTemplate.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact1 👉 Set Other Address&apos;)
),
IF({!Setup.platformEvent.Type__c} == {!Contact2_FieldApiName},
if({!Setup.formSubmission.Internal_Is_Related_Record__c},
ISPICKVAL({!Setup.pageSection.Conversion_Rule__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Other Address&apos;),
INCLUDES({!Setup.formTemplate.Conversion_Rules__c},&apos;Contact2 👉 Set Other Address&apos;)
),
false))</expression>
    </formulas>
